sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch08-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The main features of snowflake shapes are reproduced by a hexagonal cellular automaton in which a cell becomes ice only if exactly one neighbor is ice, which represents the inhibition of nearby growth by released latent heat.";
    dc:type "model-of-nature";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Snowflake shapes arise from growth inhibition captured by a hexagonal cellular automaton";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 8, “Implications for Everyday Systems”; section “The Growth of Crystals” (from p. 369), p. 370. Scope: growth of snowflakes (ice crystals from water vapor)"
}
